# Written by `vercel link` and `vercel pull` (docs/deploy.md). project.json is only ids, but
# `vercel pull` also writes the project's whole production environment - secrets included - into
# .vercel/.env.production.local, and that must never be committed.
.vercel/
*.log
.DS_Store

.env.local
apps/web/.env*.local

# generated beside the token source by an older script; the apps read packages/ui/tokens.css
assets/design-tokens.css

# Lighthouse output; CI uploads it as an artifact.
docs/lighthouse-results.json

# Written by `vercel link`. `.vercel/project.json` holds the org and project ids, and
# `vercel pull` writes the project's environment - secrets included - into
# `.vercel/.env.production.local`. The CLI also appends a blanket `.env*` every time it
# writes one of those files - `vercel link`, `vercel env pull` - and that line is removed
# each time on purpose: it lands after the env block near the top, a later pattern beats
# the earlier `!.env.example` negation, and a file this repository tracks would quietly
# join the ignore set.
.vercel/
